Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.869 align:start position:0%
 
pakistan stands  that the conflict in afghanistan  never had a military solution  was confirmed  the ideal time to end the conflict  through negotiations  might have been  when the u.s and nato troops were at  their max maximum military strength in  afghanistan  continuation of foreign military  presence for a longer duration now  would not have yielded  any positive outcome  therefore  endorsement  by the biden  administration of the previous u.s  administration's decision of troop  withdrawal  was indeed a logical conclusion  to this conflict  it is now time for the international  community to work together  to ensure an inclusive political  settlement  for a long-term peace security and  development  of afghanistan  ladies and gentlemen  pakistan  is making  active efforts  to promote  an inclusive political  settlement in afghanistan  we  at her invitation  the  leadership  of a number of political parties and  groups in afghanistan  representing all the multi-ethnic groups  apart from the pashtuns  are present in islamabad  and have met with our foreign minister  and with our leadership  today  they have promised  to engage  continuously with the taliban  and to try to invo evolve  an inclusive afghan government  pakistan will work with them  and with the taliban representatives  to advance this objective  an objective of an inclusive political  government  which is important for durable peace and  stability in afghanistan  if we had spoken in the council we would  have also informed the council of the  efforts we are making  to facilitate the safe evacuation of  diplomats  representatives of international  organization  and others from afghanistan  pakistan's foreign secretary  today briefed the diplomatic core in  islamabad  that the embassy of pakistan in kabul  will continue to facilitate visas  for diplomats and other international  personnel  whenever needed arrangements will be  made for issuing visas to such people on  arrival  a facilitation center has been set up by  our ministry in our ministry of interior  to ensure the expeditious processing of  visas and other requirements to enable  the smooth and timely evacuation from  kabul  we will try to mount  a series of flights to  kabul airport  as soon as conditions allow  in order to continue the evacuation  which we have already started  earlier today  we have evacuated a number of  people  out from the danish  embassy  421 afghan employees of the danish  embassy which we are  evacuating from from kabul  thirdly pakistan  has called upon all afghan parties  including the taliban to ensure the  preservation of law and order in kabul  and elsewhere  our immediate priority should be aimed  at the maintenance of law and order  and safety and security of all afghan  civilians especially women and children  fundamental human rights must be upheld  all civilian property and infrastructure  must be protected  they must be complete respect for human  rights  and international humanitarian law  and we support the statement of the  secretary general in this regard  fourthly the safety and security of the  diplomatic community and premises as  as well as u.n personnel humanitarian  workers and other  international staff is paramount  there is need to urgently address the  humanitarian situation in afghanistan  unama we hope will make an evaluation of  the humanitarian needs of the afghan  people we urge the u.n secretary general  to report as soon as possible on the  humanitarian needs in afghanistan in  order to mobilize emergency help through  ocha and other international agencies  we call on all afghan parties  to ensure unhindered access  and humanitarian  aid across afghanistan as well as to  ensure the safety and security of u.n  personnel and humanitarian workers  pakistan will facilitate such operations  ladies and gentlemen apart from these  immediate actions the international  community should look ahead  to other steps designed to promote  durable peace and stability in  afghanistan  the infrastructure destroyed in this  long conflict  needs to be reconstructed including the  transport infrastructure which can  enable afghanistan to serve as a hub for  regional trade and commerce  the international community also needs  to engage  with the new authorities in afghanistan  to eliminate the threat posed by  terrorist organizations  which have used afghanistan's territory  with the sponsorship of the intelligence  agencies of some of our neighbors for  attacks and sabotage against pakistan  and other  other neighbors of  afghanistan  groups such as the daesh  the ttp the jua  the etim  imu these are all organizations which  must be contained and their activities  constrained and eliminated from the  territory of afghanistan  ladies and gentlemen uh that is what i  had to say  open to your questions  ambassador  you talk about an inclusive government  for afghanistan but don't the taliban  now want to rule on their own do you  have any indication from the taliban  that they would accept an inclusive  government  and if they don't will pakistan  recognize the taliban again as the  government of afghanistan  um  i think the taliban have said  that they will accept an inclusive  government  that they would  wish to have a government which  represents  all  groups in afghanistan and we would like  to take them at that word we are working  towards that and that's why we have  invited  the representatives of the afghan  parties or the non-pashtun afghan  parties there in islam about today we're  talking to them they are agreeable to  engage with the taliban in order to  form a  inclusive  authority and we hope that our efforts  and the efforts of other friends will be  successful  michelle nichols from reuters how  important is the role of women in a new  afghanistan government and how concerned  are you by reports of  rights abuses by the taliban against  women  thank you now i i it is obvious that the  women of afghanistan  must continue to play an important role  they have demonstrated their ability to  do so and we are hopeful  that the taliban authorities and the  new inclusive government will respect  that and will enable them to play that  role the taliban statements have said  that  they will  that they are accept  girls education women  women's  working  under an islamic system  and and as you know in islam women have  equal rights and we hope that those  rights will be respected uh in any new  uh  formation in afghanistan  i'm sorry and that women should be a  part of any new government there should  be female members of a new afghan  government well we hope there will be  female members of the afghan government  it is of course for the afghans  themselves to come forward and put  forward women candidates for women  who are willing to be part of this  inclusive government but we certainly  from our part would hope  that women will be represented and will  be able to participate in the future of  afghanistan did you say you're  evacuating pakistani nationals or afghan  nationals we are evacuating  all diplomatic personnel  all diplomatic personnel who wish to  evacuate and wish to come through  pakistan  are all representatives of international  agencies  who have requested our help in being  evacuated  and all other personnel who  feel that they are in danger we would be  willing to  look at the possibility of taking them  out  so you're helping un national staff and  international staff absolutely evacuate  absolutely  we are in touch with all the  international agencies imf world bank  etc who have have offices in  kabul  and whoever wishes to leave  from the diplomatic personnel  and from the international agencies we  will process the visas sometimes some of  the visas we will issue on arrival  so we will facilitate  their evacuation  the issue of course now is kabul airport  apparently  there has been some some incidents there  so i hope that we will be able to resume  flights uh the pakistani international  airlines will arrange the flights and we  will take out people  who we process when was the last time a  flight went out from today today  so they're at the airport this morning  we evacuated personnel from the danish  mission  so the taliban is cooperating with with  pakistan on this evacuation well the  international airport as you know is  under us control now  ambassador one more question  in terms of the way pakistan sees things  the inclusive government but after that  does democracy return to afghanistan  does pakistan believe  afghanistan should still have a  democratic system  well  you know  james we have we have a democratic  system for afghanistan the final choice  is the  it's for the people of afghanistan to  choose  whether they will have what is the  system they want they want the islamic  system  uh i think they have to  talk amongst themselves and evolve what  sort of system they want it's obvious  that we will need a new constitution  will be needed and it is for them  therefore to evolve that constitution  amongst themselves and we would not wish  to dictate anything in that regard

